  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    The Rs 3 lakh budget is an assumption for illustration: use your own total for degree fees plus everything else you will spend on learning. The 10% and 20% lines are planning heuristics, not research facts. The dollar conversion uses an assumed Rs 87 per US dollar, so recheck it on the day you pay.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--amber">
    <p>
      <strong>Time is the hidden price of CFA.</strong> Three levels at about 300 hours each is 900 study hours. At 8 hours a week, that is about 112 weeks, over two years, before any retake. The CFA Institute reports a 10-year average Level I pass rate of 41%, so more than half of candidates do not pass on a given try. Only take it if you would still want the finance job after that stretch.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    The MBA sum is the biggest. Rs 17.9 lakh is 3.6 to 7.2 years of gross pay at a starting salary of Rs 5 lakh or Rs 2.5 lakh a year. The IPM's reported Rs 38.3 lakh total academic fee is 7.7 to 15.3 years of the same pay. That is why an MBA or IPM needs a named role and a placement report before you commit, not after.
  </p>

  <h2 id="mba">MBA, CAT and IPM: when the degree is worth it</h2>

  <p>
    An MBA is the most talked-about option and the most expensive one. Its value depends almost entirely on the institute.
  </p>

  <p>
    CAT 2026 is on 29 November 2026, conducted by IIM Indore. Registration closed in September. The eligibility is a bachelor's degree with at least 50% marks (45% for reserved categories), and final-year students can apply. The application fee was Rs 2,700 (Rs 1,350 for SC, ST and PwD candidates), and the deadline of 22 September 2026 was not extended. If you missed this cycle, the next one normally opens around August; check the official CAT website for the latest dates.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you are still in Class 12 and thinking of a five-year integrated route, IIM Indore's IPM charges Rs 6 lakh per year of course fee in the first three years, and its total academic fee is reported at Rs 38.3 lakh for the 2026-31 batch. IIM Indore held the 2026 entrance test on 4 May 2026. That is a very different bet from a regular BBA. Read <a href="/blog/career-options/bba-career-options/">BBA career options</a> for how the integrated route compares.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--amber">
    <p>
      <strong>A stricter test for an MBA:</strong> can you name the target role, the institute's placement report for that role, and the loan EMI against the realistic first salary? If any of the three is blank, run a proof-building stretch first. Our comparison of <a href="/blog/college-degrees/mba-vs-professional-certification-india/">MBA vs professional certification</a> shows how to think about it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="week">What a realistic BBA week can hold</h2>

  <p>
    Classes, assignments, internal exams and a part-time job leave less time than the plan on your phone. Design for the week you actually have.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>A light week (about 4-5 hours):</strong> one tool session, one small practice task, no new course.</li>
    <li><strong>A normal week (about 6-8 hours):</strong> two tool sessions plus one hour on your project.</li>
    <li><strong>Exam or placement week:</strong> pause and protect your marks. A short break does not undo your progress.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Some people finish a small project in a few weeks; others need a couple of months. Both are fine. The goal is one finished piece of proof, not a fast one.
  </p>

  <h2 id="years">A three-year BBA sequence</h2>

  <p>
    A course pick is easier when each year has one job. This is a sequence, not a deadline.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Year 1:</strong> learn Excel (lookups, pivot tables, clean formatting) and finish one small analysis on a public dataset. Test one professional syllabus by attempting a free sample paper.</li>
    <li><strong>Year 2:</strong> add SQL and a Power BI dashboard. Take the specialisation piece from the lane cards above. Finance students can sit the NISM exam now, since the certificate stays valid for 3 years, and a three-year BBA student is usually already inside the CFA Level I 23-month window by the end of year 1 (this follows from the rule; confirm at enrolment).</li>
    <li><strong>Year 3:</strong> finish the capstone project, run it through The 3 Gates, and decide between work, a professional route, or an MBA. Final-year students can apply to CAT, and the 2026 cycle opened in August.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="growth">Where the income ceiling actually moves</h2>

  <p>
    The routes above are ordered by how quickly they pay for themselves and how much room they leave to grow, not by prestige. Tools first, because a tool-led role can start within months and lets you keep learning while you earn.
  </p>

  <p>
    A salaried analyst, marketer or HR executive has a fairly fixed pay band. What raises the ceiling is a skill you can sell more widely than one employer's job description: a niche you can serve as a freelancer or consultant, a process you can systemise, or a specialism that few peers can match.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The ownership path, if you want it:</strong> analytics and marketing work can be sold as a small fixed-scope service (for example, a monthly sales dashboard for local shops, or a one-time campaign audit). It scales because you own the price and the repeatable process, and can later hire or use tools to deliver more. It needs proof, trust and client work first, so build it beside a job or internship, not instead of one.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Two multipliers sit on top of every course here. The first is clear communication, especially in English, because a good analysis nobody understands earns nothing. The second is one visible place where your work lives, such as a short portfolio page or a LinkedIn post series, so people can see your proof without asking.
  </p>

  <p>
    Two honest cautions. The exam routes carry competition at two stages: first the exam itself, then the search for the right first role or articleship. And a BBA from a college with weak placements is not a dead end, but it means your proof has to do more of the talking.
  </p>

