  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and BBA courses: what to learn now</h2>

  <p>
    AI is already good at first-draft reports, cleaning tidy data and summarising documents. That does not remove BBA roles. It moves the value to people who check the output, understand the business, and decide what to do.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Now:</strong> use an AI assistant to speed up Excel formulas, SQL queries and report drafts, and always verify the answers yourself.</li>
    <li><strong>Next:</strong> build one workflow, such as a monthly sales report that updates itself, and explain each step.</li>
    <li><strong>Later:</strong> as tools improve, the people who can design and audit these workflows will be more valuable than the people who only operate them.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Be careful with private company data and student records: never paste them into public tools. Also, "used AI" is not proof. "Used AI to build, check and improve a real report" is.
  </p>

